This package binds cmark-gfm but does not distribute it. Release 2.0
compiles nothing: the library is located on the host at import time and
loaded from wherever the system package manager put it (ADR-0015,
ADR-0016).

The notices below are reproduced because this tree ships expression
transcribed from cmark-gfm's source, not because cmark-gfm is a
development dependency:

  src/cmark/gfm/sxml.sls  the HREF_SAFE byte set, from
                          src/houdini_href_e.c:32-44   (houdini, MIT)

  src/cmark/gfm/sxml.sls  the dangerous-URL scheme rule, from
                          src/scanners.re:345-354      (cmark-gfm, BSD-3)

  tests/spec-corpus.sls   the corpus parser, from
                          test/spec_tests.py:89-126    (cmark-gfm, BSD-3)

The test software in cmark-gfm's test/ is under the same BSD-3 text, so
the one copy below covers both. src/cmark/gfm/private/native.sls also
transcribes the CMARK_OPT_* values from src/cmark-gfm.h, but those are
interface constants, not expression.

COPYING's other four blocks are absent on purpose: nothing here derives
from buffer/chunk, utf8proc, normalize.py, or the CC-BY-SA spec text.
The example corpus is read from vendor/cmark-gfm/test/ at test time and
never copied in.


